tip: | Look at the pine. | Four cones stacked, each smaller than the one below. The bottom of every cone is a piece of a 2:1 ellipse, so the tree stands on the same grid as a tile.
tip: 1 | One silhouette. | Lay out the four tiers as a jagged arrow. Getting the steps even matters more than any detail.
tip: 3 | Bands, like the barrel. | A cone is round, so each tier gets vertical bands: lit on the left, dark on the right. The same idea as the barrel, on a slant.
tip: 4 | Pick out the hems. | Light pixels along the left of each hem separate one tier from the next, and scallops stop the edge looking cut with a ruler.
